WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:06.070
Record lookup: 404. Search: still returns c_1003.

2
00:00:06.070 --> 00:00:12.330
The open results page still shows her too.

3
00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:15.390
One ID, c_1003, four homes.

4
00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:20.280
Primary table, search index, response cache, open browser.

5
00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:25.600
Flawed delete: primary row only. Outbox events: 0.

6
00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:30.260
Index and cached response still return c_1003.

7
00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:38.790
One transaction: delete the row and insert the outbox event.

8
00:00:38.790 --> 00:00:47.320
The outbox records intent. It is not atomic across destinations.

9
00:00:47.320 --> 00:00:51.890
Index entry removed. Cache invalidation fails once.

10
00:00:51.890 --> 00:00:57.110
Event stays pending. The cache still serves c_1003.

11
00:00:57.110 --> 00:01:04.790
Attempt two succeeds. Processed only after both steps.

12
00:01:04.790 --> 00:01:13.420
Replay is safe. Exhausted retries: failed state and alert.

13
00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:19.000
Backend verified: primary, index and cache are clean.

14
00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:25.740
The open page keeps its old results until it fetches again.

15
00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:28.800
After refresh: only c_1004 remains.

16
00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:35.600
Deletion is a workflow when data has more than one home.

17
00:01:35.600 --> 00:01:43.030
Not a privacy-erasure system. Backups, logs, exports, third parties: out of scope.
